research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a9-final-rem-classical-oscillator.log-2816-- **Why continuity is checked on an OPEN cover and never on the closed one.** The intervals $I_n$ form a closed cover of $(0,1]$ with infinitely many members, and the closed pasting lemma is false for infinite covers, the standing witness being [[cex-pasting-fails-for-an-infinite-closed-cover]]. The proof therefore pastes only two closed pieces at a time, producing continuity on a slightly larger closed interval, and then uses the open cover clause, which carries no finiteness restriction.
