items/thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives.md-47-2.1 By [L2], $k=f(a+h)-f(a)=O(\|h\|_2)$; boundedness of $Dg(f(a))$ and the two remainder limits show both $Dg(f(a))r_f(h)$ and $r_g(k)$ are $o(\|h\|_2)$, including the case $k=0$. [step 1.1, L2, algebra]
items/thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives.md-48-
items/thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives.md:49:3.1 Substitution into the two expansions leaves $g(f(a+h))-g(f(a))-Dg(f(a))Df(a)h=o(\|h\|_2)$, and the composite of linear maps is linear. [step 1.1, step 2.1] ∎
