research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-34-{"id":"def-pointwise-uniform-and-uniformly-cauchy-convergence","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"The definitions are correctly stated and the equivalence of real/rational error is properly justified using the Archimedean property. No mathematical error or mis-citation.","context_sha256":"a82af530353628b3599d8997063681f7adf9bd169344c214f876d58ac87bb64f","item_sha256":"00a36c5c4cbf1c8678e3222f80c07d38d8216bd35cf5941c1221ad12027b7aca","at":"2026-08-10T02:42:06.683Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-35-{"id":"thm-c-k-complete-in-the-sup-metric","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified each proof step follows from faithfully stated facts; the uniform Cauchy argument, continuous limit, and supremum-metric convergence establish completeness.","context_sha256":"37cd6e1f5a47ded36e2042aa3af00db79294023eda946f7e1eb8af2df978c4e1","item_sha256":"00fe96d13c58ed6fb4622f4cbbdbfcda5b772d68b13dd85a0baf8667e5865d83","at":"2026-08-10T02:42:09.641Z"}
