research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log-5780- - **Why the linear structure does not help.** The bisection proof of [[thm-heine-borel-rn]] halves one coordinate at a time and terminates because there are finitely many coordinates. On $V$ there are infinitely many, and the standard unit vectors stay a fixed distance apart no matter how far out one looks; that is exactly the failure of total boundedness in step 5.1.
